  "harness_epoch": 16,
  "youtube_url": "https://youtu.be/IE9BkH-cGtQ",
  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Chose to look at opponent's top card with Mishra's Bauble instead of their own. With Ponder in hand, looking at your own top card creates a well-known synergy: you'll know one of the top 3 cards when you Ponder next turn, helping you make a better decision about reordering or shuffling. Additionally, with Dragon's Rage Channeler's surveil, knowing your own top card helps decide whether to bin it for delirium progress.",
      "action_taken": "Targeted MiniMx Story (opponent) with Mishra's Bauble to look at their top card.",
      "better_line": "Target yourself with Mishra's Bauble to see your own top card, synergizing with Ponder and DRC's surveil next turn for better library manipulation decisions.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 27,
      "player": "Grok4 Diplom",
      "decision_index": 23,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Hardcasting Narcomoeba by sacrificing Lotus Petal is a questionable use of resources in a Dredge deck. Lotus Petal is a precious resource that could enable casting key spells like enabling future Dread Return or other plays. Narcomoeba is designed to come into play for free when milled. Additionally, not activating Scalding Tarn this turn means missing an opportunity to potentially fetch a land and shuffle the library, which could matter for future dredge/draw steps.",
      "action_taken": "Sacrificed Lotus Petal to hardcast Narcomoeba (a 1/1 flyer) for {1}{U}, keeping Scalding Tarn unactivated.",
      "better_line": "Consider holding Narcomoeba and Lotus Petal, using Scalding Tarn to fetch a land, and focusing on getting dredge cards (Golgari Grave-Troll or Stinkweed Imp) into the graveyard to start the dredge engine. Lotus Petal could be saved for a more impactful play later.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 34,
      "player": "MiniMx Story",
      "decision_index": 24,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Fetched Volcanic Island (U/R) when their entire hand requires black mana (Stinkweed Imp, Poxwalkers, Dread Return). They already have a Mountain for red, making the red from Volcanic Island redundant. Underground Sea would provide the black mana needed to cast Stinkweed Imp on turn 3, which is critical for getting the dredge engine started.",
      "action_taken": "Fetched Volcanic Island, giving redundant red mana and no access to black.",
      "better_line": "Fetch Underground Sea to have access to black mana for Stinkweed Imp ({2}{B}) on turn 3, enabling the dredge engine.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 42,
      "player": "MiniMx Story",
      "decision_index": 28,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Drew Cori-Steel Cutter off Ponder instead of Daze. On turn 2 with Dragon's Rage Channeler on board, Daze is significantly more valuable as free countermagic to protect DRC and disrupt the opponent's early plays. Cori-Steel Cutter requires 1R to cast and 1R to equip, making it slow, while Daze is at its best early in the game when the opponent is constrained on mana.",
      "action_taken": "Put Cori-Steel Cutter on top to draw it, burying Daze underneath",
      "better_line": "Put Daze on top to draw it, keeping free countermagic available to protect DRC and disrupt the opponent's development",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 49,
      "player": "Grok4 Diplom",
      "decision_index": 36,
    }
  ],
